spec ww04-update-rollback-then-delete: 2 sessions, 3 permutations
# WW04, rollback arm (update rolls back). s1 updates n and ROLLS BACK; the vacuum is
# drained immediately after (H1); s2 deletes n. A delete issued while s1 is open is
# refused; one issued after the rollback and drain succeeds; one committed before s1's
# write makes s1's write refused. Only interleavings with the drain adjacent to the
# rollback run.
# The second writer is an autocommit statement, so its snapshot is
# taken when it runs. An explicit transaction whose snapshot predates the ROLLBACK is
# refused even after the drain, because ExplicitTx.Rollback publishes its commit
# record instead of aborting it — a defect this catalogue found and does not pin; see
# README.md, "Defects found".

starting permutation: s1u s1rb s1dr s2d
step s1u: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 1 RETURN n.x AS x
x
-
1
(1 row)
step s1rb: ROLLBACK
step s1dr: <vacuum drain>
step s2d: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) DETACH DELETE n RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
-------
1      
(1 row)
final final: MATCH (n:Item) RETURN n.name AS name, n.x AS x ORDER BY name
name|x
----+-
"m" |0
(1 row)

starting permutation: s1u s2d s1rb s1dr
step s1u: MATCH (n:Item {name:'n'}) SET n.x = 1 RETURN n.x AS x
x
